<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Boyacá</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1819</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-wars-of-independence">Spanish American wars of independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boyaca-department">Boyacá</a> was fought on 7 August 1819 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunja">Tunja</a> in present-day Colombia, where the patriot army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-de-paula-santander">Francisco de Paula Santander</a> defeated a royalist force after crossing the Andes. The victory opened the road to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a>, ended Spanish rule over most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a> and led to the proclamation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a> Colombia later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-boyaca.jpg" alt="Battle of Boyacá" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martin Tovar y Tovar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batalla_de_Boyaca_de_Martin_Tovar_y_Tovar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
